title: Cuno Falls
subtitle: The government resigns. The strike must end, or go further.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_cuno = 1 and (e23_cuno_pressure >= 100 or e23_cuno_endurance <= 0 or crisis_time >= 4)
max-visits: 1
priority: 4
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.cunoTick(Q.crisis_time);
var p = Q.e23_cuno_pressure, e = Q.e23_cuno_endurance;
Q.e23_cuno_result = p >= 100 ? (e >= 30 ? 1 : 2) : (e <= 0 ? 3 : (p >= 70 ? 2 : 3));
Q.e23_cuno_can_rise = (Q.e23_cuno_result == 1 || (Q.e23_cuno_result == 2 && Q.e23_cuno_aim == 3)) && Q.e23_cuno_spd != 1 ? 1 : 0;
RG.news('Cuno resigns: Stresemann forms a great coalition', 3);
Q.chancellor = 'Gustav Stresemann';
Q.government_name = 'Stresemann cabinet (DVP, Centre, DDP, SPD)';
Q.spd_in_government = 1; Q.zentrum_in_government = 1; Q.ddp_in_government = 1; Q.dvp_in_government = 1; Q.bvp_in_government = 0;
Q.stability += 4;
Q.e23_cuno_done = 1;
!}

= Cuno Falls

On 12 August Wilhelm Cuno resigns. The next day Gustav Stresemann of the People's Party forms a great coalition from his own party to the SPD. The Social Democrats get four ministries, finance among them, and promise a stable currency.

[? if e23_cuno_result = 1 : The strike is not over. The factory councils are still in session, the hundreds stand at the power stations, and the police are waiting for orders that do not come. ?][? if e23_cuno_result = 2 : The strike has done what it set out to do, and it is ebbing works by works. The party has led three million workers and brought down a government. ?][? if e23_cuno_result = 3 : The strike was breaking before Cuno fell. The strikers went back when their families could hold out no longer, and the government's fall looks like the SPD's work. ?][? if e23_cuno_spd = 1 : We promised the SPD that the strike would end with Cuno. ?]

- @rising: Turn the strike into a rising.
- @victory: End the strike in good order.
- @over: The strike is over.

@rising
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The German revolution in August, without a plan and without asking Moscow.
view-if: e23_cuno_can_rise = 1
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('uprising');
RG.ecci('radek', -6);
RG.ecci('bukharin', 6);
RG.ledger('The Cuno strike became a rising, without a plan and without Moscow.', 'e23_cuno_rising');
RG.news('Hundreds seize Berlin power stations', 3);
Q.e23_october_path = 2;
var s = RG.e22.striking();
RG.e22.octRise(s.length ? s : ['berlin'], 'The German Revolution', 'Hold the districts that have risen until the Reichswehr breaks.', Q.e23_council_congress ? 2 : 0);
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
Q.independence += 5;
!}

The council of the Berlin works calls on the workers to arm. The hundreds take the power station at Klingenberg and the junctions at Lichtenberg, and in Dresden and Hamburg the district leaders open the arms stores. The Reichswehr ministry declares a state of siege.

@victory
subtitle: The party's name is made, and many strikers join.
view-if: e23_cuno_result <= 2
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.striking().forEach(function (d) { RG.endStrike(d, 'won'); });
RG.e22.cunoClear();
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 8);
RG.ecci('trotsky', 6);
RG.ledger('The Cuno strike, led by the party, brought down the government.', 'e23_cuno_won');
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.08;
}
Q.worker_support += 5;
!}

The councils vote to return to work on 14 August. Tens of thousands join the party in the following weeks. In Moscow Zinoviev reads the reports and starts to talk about a German October.

@over
subtitle: The party keeps its organisation, and little else.
view-if: e23_cuno_result = 3
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.striking().forEach(function (d) { RG.endStrike(d, 'quiet'); });
RG.e22.cunoClear();
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -4);
Q.worker_support -= 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 6;
!}

The last strike committees dissolve. The police release most of the arrested delegates within the week, and the Left says the party ran away from its own strike.
